{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2950,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're all familiar with gravity as \"the reason\nobjects fall\", but there's much, much more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7160,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to gravity than that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9350,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity is a long range attractive force between\nall objects with mass:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12890,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's what keeps us from falling off the earth,\nit's what keeps the earth in orbit around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16120,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sun, and it's what caused the sun itself\nto form four and a half billion years ago!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20800,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's amazing to think that every massive object\nattracts every other in the universe –"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24390,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that means that your dog, the earth,\nand a black hole in the Andromeda galaxy 2.5"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28940,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million light years away\nare all gravitationally attracted to you,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32930,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you to them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34020,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 17th century, Isaac Newton discovered\nthat the strength of the gravitational force"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38050,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "decreases by the square of the distance between\ntwo objects – so if you're twice as far"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42720,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "away, gravity is only one fourth as strong!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45760,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He also discovered that the strength of gravity\nis proportional to the mass of the objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in question: the more massive an object, the\nstronger the gravitational force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54440,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why we can all feel the Earth pulling\non us, but don't really notice the pull of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58300,
    "dDurationMs": 2279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the moon – it's smaller, and farther away!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60579,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(the moon's gravity is strong enough to cause\nthe tides, though!)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64390,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when I said earlier that gravity is an\nattraction between objects with mass, I lied."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68409,
    "dDurationMs": 1901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I meant objects with Energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70310,
    "dDurationMs": 4489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because in addition to massive objects, gravity\nalso attracts light and other massless (but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74799,
    "dDurationMs": 4051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energetic) particles, so that a photon of\nlight can be bent slightly passing the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78850,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or trapped completely by a black hole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81810,
    "dDurationMs": 1989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now do you understand the Gravity of the situation?"
    } ]
  } ]
}
